  "head": "working-tree",
  "subject": "Borrowed SharedChannel duplex writes",
  "change": "SharedChannel writers gain writeBorrowedMessage and writeFinalBorrowedMessage. The endpoint owner stages caller-owned prefix-reserved identity storage without copying and still writes it in bounded max_write_bytes_per_turn turns, preserving per-endpoint fairness. Borrowed writes wait for owner completion instead of abandoning the buffer; owner-side deadline or stream failure completes the command before the caller returns. Compression still allocates a separate framed buffer owned by the stream, and pending-message ownership now records whether the transport may free the bytes.",
  "tests": {
